    "updated_at": "2022-02-15T03:37:21Z",
    "body": "I guess that's true (and now that you mention it, that's started bugging me a little), but my point is that the normative text doesn't match what seems to be the intended behavior. As I noted in the edit, the grammar as written allows the parser to match unbalanced parentheses, brackets, and braces in extended attributes, at least in the super-permissive _ExtendedAttributeList_ rule. It probably doesn't change any actual behavior, since extended attributes undergo more parsing later on, but I think it's still worth fixing.\r\n\r\nIn retrospect, I buried the lead a little. I'm changing the issue name to better reflect the problem.",
